.TH PRJ 1 "2026-10-05" "prj 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prj \- pick a project from a list and open it in your agent, editor or shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prj
.RI [ query ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR command ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR args... ]
.br
.B prj
.BR \-p | \-l
.RI [ query ]
.br
.B prj
.BR \-\-setup | \-\-doctor | \-\-edit | \-\-uninstall
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prj
lists the git repositories found in your project folders and opens the one you pick.
Without a query it shows an
.BR fzf (1)
picker with a git log and status preview. With a query it opens the project whose name matches exactly, or the
only fuzzy match, or the picker filtered by the query.
.PP
Projects are sorted with pinned ones first, then by how often and how recently you opened them, then by the
date of their last commit. Repositories nested inside another repository are not listed.
.PP
Opening a project types the configured
.I run
command into an interactive shell in the project folder, so shell aliases and functions work.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " mode" "\fR, \fP\-\-open " mode
Where to open the project:
.B auto
(a new herdr tab or tmux window when running inside one, otherwise the current terminal),
.BR herdr\-tab ,
.BR tmux\-window ,
or
.BR here .
.TP
.BI \-r " command" "\fR, \fP\-\-run " command
Run this instead of the configured command.
.TP
.BI \-\- " args..."
Append these arguments, quoted, to the run command.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path
Print the project path instead of opening it.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List projects.
.B \-\-tsv
prints name, branch, last commit date, path and a pinned flag, separated by tabs.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Run the setup wizard: choose project folders, the run command, the open mode and the names of the shell commands
to install. Re-running it edits the existing configuration. With
.BR \-\-yes ,
it uses detected or existing values; each answer also has a flag:
.BR \-\-roots ,
.BR \-\-run ,
.BR \-\-open ,
.BR \-\-name ,
.BR \-\-cd\-name ,
.BR \-\-no\-shell ,
.BR \-\-no\-skill .
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check dependencies, project folders and shell integration.
.TP
.B \-\-edit
Open the configuration file in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove the shell hooks, shell files and Claude Code skill that setup added. The configuration and usage history
are kept.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/prj/config
Settings:
.BR roots ,
.BR depth ,
.BR run ,
.BR open ,
.BR pinned ,
.BR exclude ,
.BR name ,
.BR cd_name .
Lists are comma separated.
.TP
.I ~/.config/prj/shell.sh
Shell functions and completion, loaded from
.I ~/.bashrc
or
.IR ~/.zshrc .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/prj/history
Usage history used for sorting.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/skills/repo/SKILL.md
Claude Code skill installed by setup.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PRJ_CONFIG
Use a different configuration file.
.TP
.B PRJ_STATE_DIR
Directory for the usage history.
.TP
.B PRJ_SCAN_MOUNTS
Directories whose subfolders setup scans for mounted drives.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors such as an unknown or ambiguous query without a terminal, 130 when the picker is cancelled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fzf (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR tmux (1)
